-- comments
1:1 plain -- A comment in a hole runs to the end of its line, `}` included
2:1 plain -- (frontend.md §9.1): `{-- note}` leaves the hole open, so the `</p>` on the
3:1 plain -- next line is lexed as code in the hole, and the column-1 `after` ends the
4:1 plain -- markup. The comment is listed like any other, and the hole is one
5:1 plain -- unclosed_delimiter at its `{` (8:8), whose message quotes the comment and
6:1 plain -- shows the two-line spelling (frontend.md §9.5).
8:9 plain -- note}
